+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts a JSON object with a `csv` string and the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. Each row gives an ISO instant with a time zone and a
+  positive whole number of portions. Success returns `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 3 }`
+  for one newly imported ticket containing three portions. Previously imported
+  tickets are skipped. A bad row or insufficient stock rejects the whole file
+  and the error names the CSV row (header is row 1).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array ordered
+  by item ID for the inclusive UTC date range. Each row contains `itemId`,
+  `theoretical` (recipe use from sales), `actual` (all ledger consumption), and
+  `variance` (actual minus theoretical), in the item's unit. Items with zero
+  use in both columns are omitted.
